2026-05-03T17:02:10.682Z JOY-0157-86 comment.added "Plan: (1) joy-crypt: add x25519-dalek + curve25519-dalek deps; identity::Keypair gains to_x25519_secret() and PublicKey gains to_x25519_public() via Ed25519->Montgomery conversion. New pairwise module with pairwise_kek(my_x25519_secret, peer_x25519_public, info) -> [u8; 32] doing ECDH + HKDF. (2) joy-core/crypt: change wrap format to include granter's verify_key as a prefix; wrap_for_member uses pairwise_kek with the granter's secret + recipient's public; unwrap_for_member reads the granter prefix, looks up their public key, derives the symmetric pairwise KEK with own secret + granter's public, decrypts. Self-wrap (auto-create) is the special case granter==recipient. (3) joy-cli/commands/crypt: implement run_grant using the new primitive. (4) Tests: pairwise self/cross roundtrip, recipient cannot decrypt without granter pubkey, third party cannot decrypt." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
